  "changed_since_previous": "No functional differences; patch rebased or re-formatted.",
  "card": "Bounds descriptor key expansion during import top-ups to start at range_start rather than index 0, and records the derived index directly. Currently, importing a descriptor with range [N, M] derives and caches all keys from 0 to M, making import cost O(M) instead of O(M - N) and causing keys below N to appear as owned during import only to disappear when the wallet is reloaded. The author reports that importing a 10-key range starting at index 600,000 drops from 19.5 seconds to 0.09 seconds, and prevents pathological large range starts from attempting to derive up to 2^31 keys.",
